<h1>For A Friend's 53rd Birthday</h1><br/><br/><strong>
<br/>
On looking forward to the fourth day of November<br/>
I faithfully desire to take time to fondly remember<br/>
The birthday of a dedicated priest and dear friend<br/>
And i wish him God 's Love for always, without end.<br/>
I pray for passing angels to comfort him to be at peace<br/>
In the dank, cold darkness when doubts fail to cease.<br/>
I pray that he will see God's magnificent Beauty in Creation <br/>
Even in the midst of&nbsp;&nbsp;man's most horrendous abomination.<br/>
I pray to the Holy Spirit to nourish him so that he is content<br/>
In knowing his life of serving as a shepherd is one well spent.<br/>
I hope he knows that his contribution to my being remains<br/>
As a flame buring golden in a heart opened and unchained<br/>
May our fairest Mother Mary wrap her cloak, so warm and blue<br/>
Around him snugly so that he may feel her Love, born and true<br/>
<br/>
Happy fifty-third Birthday and feast day of your patron<br/>
May your soul be sweetly illuminated by the Risen Son!		<br/>
</strong>
